# SlayZone Env Vars — Standalone Hub & Runner

Every var surfaced by the full 4-cluster deep-dive, assessed for the standalone deploy surface. Dev/build/e2e/internal vars summarized at bottom.

**Precedence everywhere:** `env var > SLAYZONE_RUNNER_CONFIG file (runner) > ~/.slayzone/config.json > generated/default`

**Two axes.** Paths key off `SLAYZONE_SUPERVISED` (Electron host injects env vs process resolves own) → the two Default columns. Auth keys off **exposure** (`SLAYZONE_HOST` non-loopback) → derived, not a column. Deriving auth from *supervised* would break the standalone-but-loopback fork sidecar — don't.

**Single anchor.** `SLAYZONE_ROOT` (renamed from `SLAYZONE_HOME_DIR`) anchors hub + runner; config.json, DB, logs, creds all derive. Default CWD (standalone) / `$HOME/.slayzone` (supervised). Relocate = `cd /srv/slayzone && slayzone-hub`.
```
SLAYZONE_ROOT ── slayzone.sqlite · config.json · logs/ · runner/(creds)
```

**Minimize legend:** 🟢 keep (operator sets) · 🔵 derive (process computes, not a knob) · 🟠 hide (subsumed by token; advanced override only) · 🔴 delete

